From d3f1fcb404ae36b4fb8cc8d1ec35b00b057586fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:36:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] steam-frame client: go back to SteamVR home when the app on
 the Mac is gone

The headset kept showing the app's last frame after the app quit or crashed, which reads as a freeze.

- On the server's stream-end marker (VIDEO_FLAG_STREAM_END) the client disconnects and looks for the server for
  5 s, since xrEndSession sends it too and an app may begin a new session; if none comes back it ends its
  session (the Ctrl-C path: xrRequestExitSession, exit 0), SteamVR shows its home, and the launcher's unit does
  not restart it (it restarts on status 4 only).
- A crashed app sends no marker: FRAME_CLIENT_APP_GONE_S seconds (default 20, 0 = marker only) with no video,
  after video had started on the connection, end the session the same way.

Tested 10-28 on the stand: Unreal SIGTERM (RequestExit) -> marker, home 6 s after the quit; Godot SIGTERM (no
teardown) -> home on the 20 s rule. 742 unit checks green.

